===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*deyḱ-}}
From {{der|en|la|index|t=a discoverer, informer, spy; of things, an indicator, the forefinger, a title, superscription}}, from {{m|la|indicō|t=point out, show}}; see {{m|en|indicate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪndɛks/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-index.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|indices|index's|pl3qual=obsolete, in use in the 17th century}}

# An [[alphabetical]] [[listing]] of [[item]]s and their [[location]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''index''' of a book lists words or expressions and the pages of the book upon which they are to be found.}}
# The [[index finger]]; the [[forefinger]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:index finger}}
# A [[movable]] [[finger]] on a [[gauge]], [[scale]], etc.
# {{lb|en|typography}} A [[symbol]] [[resemble|resembling]] a [[point]]ing [[hand]], used to [[direct]] particular [[attention]] to a [[note]] or [[paragraph]].
#: {{syn|en|manicule}}
# That which [[point]]s [[out]]; that which [[show]]s, [[indicate]]s, [[manifest]]s, or [[disclose]]s.
#* {{RQ:Arbuthnot Aliments
|passage=Tastes are the '''Indexes''' of the different Qualities of Plants.}}
# A [[sign]]; an [[indication]]; a [[token]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1887|author=w:Robert Louis Stevenson|title=The Misadventures of John Nicholson
|passage=His son's empty guffaws {{...}} struck him with pain as the '''indices''' of a weak mind.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=22 Dec 84|volume=12|number=23|journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Gayle Rubin|title=Censored: Anti-Porn Laws And Women's Liberation|text=Their use of these words as epithets is an '''index''' of an appallingly low level  of feminist awareness.}}
# {{lb|en|linguistics}} A type of [[noun]] where the [[meaning]] of the [[form]] [[change]]s with respect to the [[context]]; e.g., 'Today's newspaper' is an indexical form since its [[referent]] will differ depending on the context. See also [[icon]] and [[symbol]].
# {{lb|en|economics}} A [[single]] [[number]] [[calculate]]d from an [[array]] of [[price]]s or of [[quantity|quantities]].
# {{lb|en|science}} A [[number]] [[represent]]ing a [[property]] or [[ratio]]; a [[coefficient]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=w:Richard Feynman|title=w:The Feynman Lectures on Physics| volume=I| chapter=Chapter 26, Optics: The Principle of Least Time| chapterurl= http://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/I_26.html| passage=In other words, we predict that the '''index''' for a new pair of materials can be obtained from the '''indexes''' of the individual materials, both against air or against vacuum.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[raised]] [[suffix]] [[indicate|indicating]] a [[power]].
# {{lb|en|computing|especially|programming|and|databases}} An [[integer]] or other [[key]] [[indicate|indicating]] the [[location]] of [[data]], e.g. within an [[array]], [[vector]], [[database]] [[table]], [[associative array]], or [[hash table]].
# {{lb|en|computing|databases}} A [[data structure]] that [[improve]]s the [[performance]] of [[operation]]s on a [[table]].
# {{lb|en|algebra|index of a subgroup}} The number of [[coset]]s that exist.
#: {{ux|en|The '''index''' of 2ℤ in ℤ is 2.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[prologue]] [[indicate|indicating]] what [[follow]]s.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|III|4|text=Ay me, what act, that roars so loud and thunders in the '''index'''?}}

